# Rule Manager

## File locations
| Type | Location | Naming |
|---|---|---|
| Always rule | `.cursor/rules/core-rules/` | `*-always.mdc` |
| Auto-attached | `.cursor/rules/{category}/` | `*-auto.mdc` |
| Agent-requested | `.cursor/rules/{category}/` | `*-agent.mdc` |
| Skill | `.cursor/skills/{name}/SKILL.md` | — |
| Command | `.cursor/commands/{name}.md` | — |

## Categories
- `core-rules/` — architecture, global contracts, agent behavior
- `api-rules/` — controllers, DTOs, requests, router
- `service-rules/` — services, domain models, GORM queries
- `database-rules/` — DB models, migrations, connection
- `logging-rules/` — logging patterns and obligations
- `security-rules/` — auth, middleware, validation
- `config-rules/` — env variables, configuration

## Rules
- Before creating a rule, check if an existing rule already covers the pattern
- After changing architecture (router path, API version, DB model folder), **verify paths against the repo** — stale paths break agent guidance
- Keep each .mdc file under ~250 lines — split if needed
- Never add content to `project-architecture-always` unless it's truly global
- After any creation or update: `✅ .cursor/rules/{path}/{file}.mdc created/updated`
- All authored content under `.cursor/` must be **English** (chat summaries to the user may use French if the team prefers)

## Globs vs descriptions (attachment)

- **`globs` frontmatter** — use **unquoted** values: `globs: database/model/**/*.go`. Do **not** write `globs: "database/model/**/*.go"`.
- **Tight globs** — attach auto rules to the smallest path that needs enforcement (e.g. `application/**/*.go`, `services/**/client.go`), not `**/*.go` unless truly universal.
- **keyword-rich `description`** — include folders (`controllers/v1`, `middleware`), symbols (`CTRLogger`, `GORM`, `Supabase`), and phrases like "when wiring imports in application layer" so rules surface via @-mention / retrieval when the open file does not match the glob.
- **`alwaysApply: true`** — only for repo-wide maps (e.g. `project-architecture-always.mdc`); do not widen other rules to compensate.
- **Overlap** — if two rules would attach on the same edit, narrow one glob or merge guidance into a single file to avoid duplicate context.
- **No `app/` prefix** — this stack uses a flat layout at repo root; globs and paths must not reference an `app/` wrapper folder.
